<p id="mwBA"><b id="mwBQ">Eran Elinav</b> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Hebrew_language" title="Hebrew language" about="#mwt5" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Langx","href":"./Template:Langx"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"he"},"2":{"wt":"ערן אלינב"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwBg">Hebrew</a><span about="#mwt5">: </span><span lang="he" dir="rtl" about="#mwt5">ערן אלינב</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_Hebrew-language_text" about="#mwt5" id="mwBw"/>; born 22 June 1969 in Jerusalem, Israel) is an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Israelis" title="Israelis" id="mwCA">Israeli</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Immunologist" title="Immunologist" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCQ">immunologist</a><sup about="#mwt8" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nature_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nature"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-nature-1"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-nature-1" id="mwCg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQ">]</span></span></a></sup><!--<ref name="BBC"&#x3E;{{cite news |last1=Brown |first1=Jessica |title=What we do and don't know about gut health |url=https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20190121&#x2D;what&#x2D;we&#x2D;do&#x2D;and&#x2D;dont&#x2D;know&#x2D;about&#x2D;gut&#x2D;health |accessdate=22 July 2020 |publisher=[[BBC]] |date=22 January 2019}}</ref&#x3E;<ref name="theguardian"&#x3E;{{cite news |last1=Davis |first1=Nicola KS |title=Vaginal fluid transplants could cure bacterial vaginosis |url=https://www.theguardian.com/society/2019/oct/07/vaginal&#x2D;fluid&#x2D;transplants&#x2D;could&#x2D;cure&#x2D;bacterial&#x2D;vaginosis |accessdate=22 July 2020 |publisher=[[The guardian]] |date=7 October 2019}}</ref&#x3E;<ref name="globes"&#x3E;{{cite news |title=Probiotics can be worse than useless, Israeli scientists find |url=https://en.globes.co.il/en/article&#x2D;probiotics&#x2D;may&#x2D;be&#x2D;worse&#x2D;than&#x2D;useless&#x2D;israeli&#x2D;scientists&#x2D;find&#x2D;1001253002 |accessdate=22 July 2020 |publisher=[[Globes]] |date=6 September 2018}}</ref&#x3E; --> and microbiota researcher<sup about="#mwt9" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-JEM_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"JEM"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-JEM-2" id="mwDg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEA">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQ">]</span></span></a></sup><!-- <ref name="haaretz"&#x3E;{{cite news |last1=Reisfeld |first1=Smadar |title=Which Foods Make You Fat? The Answer Is in Your Gut |url=https://www.haaretz.com/science&#x2D;and&#x2D;health/MAGAZINE&#x2D;which&#x2D;foods&#x2D;are&#x2D;bad&#x2D;for&#x2D;you&#x2D;the&#x2D;answer&#x2D;is&#x2D;in&#x2D;your&#x2D;gut&#x2D;1.5403241 |accessdate=22 July 2020 |publisher=[[Haaretz]] |date=11 February 2016}}</ref&#x3E; --> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Weizmann_Institute_of_Science" title="Weizmann Institute of Science" id="mwEg">Weizmann Institute of Science</a><sup about="#mwt10" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ElinavLab_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ElinavLab"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-ElinavLab-3" id="mwEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFg">]</span></span></a></sup><!-- <ref name="indiatimes"&#x3E;{{cite news |last1=Akhter |first1=Shahid |title=Blood sugar levels response to food are highly individualized: Dr Eran Elinav |url=https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/blood&#x2D;sugar&#x2D;levels&#x2D;response&#x2D;to&#x2D;food&#x2D;are&#x2D;highly&#x2D;individualized&#x2D;/70099863 |accessdate=22 July 2020 |publisher=[[Indiatimes]] |date=6 July 2019}}</ref&#x3E;<ref name="israel21c"&#x3E;{{cite news |last1=Klein Leichman |first1=Abigail |title=Is the microbiome about to change medicine for good? |url=https://www.israel21c.org/is&#x2D;the&#x2D;microbiome&#x2D;about&#x2D;to&#x2D;change&#x2D;medicine&#x2D;for&#x2D;good/ |accessdate=22 July 2020 |publisher=israel21c |date=15 October 2019}}</ref&#x3E; --> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./German_Cancer_Research_Center" title="German Cancer Research Center" id="mwFw">German Cancer Research Center</a>.<sup about="#mwt11" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-DKFZ_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"DKFZ"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-DKFZ-4" id="mwGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGw">]</span></span></a></sup>  He is an international scholar at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Howard_Hughes_Medical_Institute" title="Howard Hughes Medical Institute" id="mwHA">Howard Hughes Medical Institute</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Bill_&amp;_Melinda_Gates_Foundation" title="Bill &amp; Melinda Gates Foundation" class="mw-redirect" id="mwHQ">Bill &amp; Melinda Gates Foundation</a>,<sup about="#mwt14" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HHMI_5-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HHMI"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HHMI-5"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-HHMI-5" id="mwHg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIA">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIQ">]</span></span></a></sup> a senior fellow of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Canadian_Institute_for_Advanced_Research" title="Canadian Institute for Advanced Research" id="mwIg">Canadian Institute for Advanced Research</a>,<sup about="#mwt17" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CIFAR_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CIFAR"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CIFAR-6"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-CIFAR-6" id="mwIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJQ">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJg">]</span></span></a></sup> and a partner at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Novo_Nordisk_Foundation" title="Novo Nordisk Foundation" id="mwJw">Novo Nordisk Foundation</a> Microbiome Health Initiative.<sup about="#mwt20" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Novo_7-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Novo"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Novo-7"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-Novo-7" id="mwKA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKg">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}' id="mwLA"/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwLQ"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Academic_and_medical_career">Academic and medical career</h2>

<p id="mwLg">Elinav earned a M.D. from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Hebrew_University_of_Jerusalem" title="Hebrew University of Jerusalem" id="mwLw">Hebrew University in Jerusalem</a> in 1999.<sup about="#mwt23" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:7_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":7"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:7-8"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:7-8" id="mwMA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMg">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMw">]</span></span></a></sup> Following an internship and residency in internal medicine at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Hadassah_Medical_Center" title="Hadassah Medical Center" id="mwNA">Hadassah-Hebrew University Medical Center</a> in 2000–2004.<sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:7_8-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":7"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:7-8" id="mwNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup></p><!-- <ref&#x3E;{{cite web |title=Scientific founders |url=https://www.biomx.com/about/ |website=biomx |accessdate=22 July 2020}}</ref&#x3E; -->

<p id="mwOQ">He served as a senior physician-scientist at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Tel_Aviv_Sourasky_Medical_Center" title="Tel Aviv Sourasky Medical Center" id="mwOg">Tel Aviv Sourasky Medical Center</a> Institute of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Gastroenterology" title="Gastroenterology" id="mwOw">Gastroenterology</a> and Liver Disease in 2005–2009.<sup about="#mwt27" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-JEM_2-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"JEM"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-JEM-2"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-JEM-2" id="mwPA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPw">]</span></span></a></sup></p><!-- <ref&#x3E;{{cite web |title=les probiotiques sont&#x2D;ils vraiment efficaces ? |url=https://www.israelscienceinfo.com/medecine/weizmann&#x2D;israel&#x2D;les&#x2D;probiotiques&#x2D;sont&#x2D;ils&#x2D;vraiment&#x2D;efficaces/ |website=Israel Science Info |accessdate=22 July 2020}}</ref&#x3E; -->

<p id="mwQA">In 2009 Elinav earned a Ph.D. in immunology from the <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.weizmann.ac.il/" class="external text" id="mwQQ">Weizmann Institute of Science</a>, advised by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Zelig_Eshhar" title="Zelig Eshhar" id="mwQg">Zelig Eshhar</a>, after developing the Chimeric Antigen Receptor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Regulatory_T_cell" title="Regulatory T cell" id="mwQw">Regulatory T cell</a> (CAR-Treg) approach,<sup about="#mwt30" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-9"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-9" id="mwRA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwRQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRg">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRw">]</span></span></a></sup> as treatment of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Inflammatory_bowel_diseases" title="Inflammatory bowel diseases" class="mw-redirect" id="mwSA">inflammatory bowel disease</a> and autoimmunity. In 2009-2012 he 
followed by a post-doc at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Yale_University" title="Yale University" id="mwSQ">Yale University</a>, advised by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Richard_A._Flavell" title="Richard A. Flavell" id="mwSg">Richard Anthony Flavell</a>, in which he discovered the NLRP6 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Inflammasome" title="Inflammasome" id="mwSw">inflammasome</a>.<sup about="#mwt33" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-10"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-10" id="mwTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTg">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwUA">In 2012 Elinav moved to the Weizmann Institute of Science and in 2016 was made a professor.<sup about="#mwt36" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ElinavLab_3-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ElinavLab"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ElinavLab-3"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-ElinavLab-3" id="mwUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVA">]</span></span></a></sup>
He heads the Institute of Microbiome research<sup about="#mwt39" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-11" id="mwVQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWA">]</span></span></a></sup> and the Center of Host-Pathogen Interaction Research at the Weizmann Institute of Science and the Microbiome &amp; Cancer Division at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./German_Cancer_Research_Center" title="German Cancer Research Center" id="mwWQ">German Cancer Research Center</a>.<sup about="#mwt42" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-DKFZ_4-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"DKFZ"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-DKFZ-4"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-DKFZ-4" id="mwWg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXA">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXQ">]</span></span></a></sup> He is the head of the <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.weizmann.ac.il/immunology/" class="external text" id="mwXg">Department of Systems Immunology</a> at the Weizmann Institute of Science.<sup about="#mwt45" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-12"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-12" id="mwXw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwYA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYQ">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwYw"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Research">Research</h2>
<p id="mwZA">Elinav studies the molecular basis of host-microbiota interactions,<sup about="#mwt48" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-13"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-13" id="mwZQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZw">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaA">]</span></span></a></sup> and the effects of diet,<sup about="#mwt51" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-14"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-14" id="mwaQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaw">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt54" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_15-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:3-15"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:3-15" id="mwbQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbw">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcA">]</span></span></a></sup> environmental factors,<sup about="#mwt57" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:5_16-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":5"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:5-16"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:5-16" id="mwcQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcw">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdA">]</span></span></a></sup> immune function<sup about="#mwt60" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_17-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:6-17"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:6-17" id="mwdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mweA">]</span></span></a></sup><!-- <ref name=":7"&#x3E;{{cite journal | last1 = Gury Ben | first1 = Ari M | last2 = Thaiss | first2 = CA | last3 = Winter | first3 = DR | last4 = Lara&#x2D;Astiaso | first4 = D | last5 = Giladi | first5 = A | last6 = Weiner | first6 = A | last7 = David | first7 = E | last8 = Shapiro | first8 = H | last9 = Dori&#x2D;Bachash | first9 = M | last10 = Pevsner&#x2D;Fischer | first10 = M | last11 = Lorenzo&#x2D;Vivas | first11 = E | last12 = Keren&#x2D;Shaul | first12 = H | last13 = Paul | first13 = F | last14 = Harmelin | first14 = A | last15 = Eberl | first15 = G | last16 = Tanay | first16 = A | last17 = Elinav | first17 = E | last18 = Amit | first18 = I | year = 2016 | title = Reconstructing the spectrum and regulatory landscapes of innate lymphoid cells in homeostasis and dysbiosis | url = | journal = Cell | volume = 166 | issue = 5| pages = 1231–1246 | pmid = 27545347 | doi = 10.1016/j.cell.2016.07.043 }}</ref&#x3E; --> and host genetics<sup about="#mwt63" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_18-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:8-18"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:8-18" id="mweQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mweg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwew">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfA">]</span></span></a></sup> on the intestinal microbiome and associated multi-factorial metabolic,<sup about="#mwt66" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-19" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-19"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-19" id="mwfQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfw">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt69" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-20" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-20"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-20" id="mwgQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgw">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhA">]</span></span></a></sup> inflammatory,<sup about="#mwt70" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TimurT_21-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TimurT"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-TimurT-21" id="mwhQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwhg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhw">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiA">]</span></span></a></sup> malignant<sup about="#mwt73" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-22" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-22"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-22" id="mwiQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiw">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjA">]</span></span></a></sup> and neurogenerative disease.<sup about="#mwt76" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-23" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-23"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-23" id="mwjQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjw">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt79" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:10_24-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":10"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:10-24"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:10-24" id="mwkQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwkg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkw">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlA">]</span></span></a></sup>
His most-cited papers have more than 2,000 cites each.<sup about="#mwt82" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-25" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-25"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-25" id="mwlQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwlg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlw">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwmA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwmQ">Elinav developed precision microbiota interventions, including personalized nutrition,<sup about="#mwt85" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_26-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-26"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:0-26" id="mwmg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwmw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnA">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt86" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_27-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:1-27" id="mwng"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwnw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwoA">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwoQ">]</span></span></a></sup> precision probiotics,<sup about="#mwt87" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-28" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-28"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-28" id="mwog"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpA">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpQ">]</span></span></a></sup><!-- <ref name="newreview&#x3E;{{cite journal | last1 = Zmora | first1 = N | last2 = Suez | first2 = J | last3 = Elinav | first3 = E | year = 2019 | title = [https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591&#x2D;019&#x2D;0439&#x2D;x The pros, the cons and many unknowns of probiotics]. 2019 | url = | journal = Nature Medicine | volume = 25 | issue = 5| pages = 716–29 | pmid = 31061539 | doi = 10.1038/s41591&#x2D;019&#x2D;0439&#x2D;x }}</ref&#x3E; --> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Small_molecule" title="Small molecule" id="mwpg">small molecule</a> ″postbiotics″,<sup about="#mwt88" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_15-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:3-15" id="mwpw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwqA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqQ">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqg">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Phage_therapy" title="Phage therapy" id="mwqw">phage therapy</a>,<sup about="#mwt91" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BiomX_29-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BiomX"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BiomX-29"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-BiomX-29" id="mwrA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwrQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrg">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt94" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IBD_phage_therapy_30-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"IBD phage therapy"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-IBD_phage_therapy-30"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-IBD_phage_therapy-30" id="mwsA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwsQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsg">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsw">]</span></span></a></sup><!-- <ref name=:14&#x3E;{{Cite journal|last1=Akamatsu|first1=N.|last2=Nakajima|first2=H.|last3=Ono|first3=M.|last4=Miura|first4=Y.|date=1975&#x2D;09&#x2D;15|title=Increase in acetyl CoA synthetase activity after phenobarbital treatment|url=https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/15|journal=Biochemical Pharmacology|volume=24|issue=18|pages=1725–1727|doi=10.1016/0006&#x2D;2952(75)90013&#x2D;1|issn=0006&#x2D;2952|pmid=15}}</ref&#x3E; --> autologous fecal microbiome transplantation,<sup about="#mwt97" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-31" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-31"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-31" id="mwtA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtg">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt100" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:13_32-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":13"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:13-32"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:13-32" id="mwuA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwuQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwug">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuw">]</span></span></a></sup> vaginal microbiome transplantation<sup about="#mwt103" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-33" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-33"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-33" id="mwvA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvg">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt106" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:15_34-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":15"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:15-34"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:15-34" id="mwwA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwwQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwg">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwww">]</span></span></a></sup> and gut epithelial<sup about="#mwt109" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:16_35-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":16"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:16-35"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:16-35" id="mwxA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxg">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt110" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-36" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-36"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-36" id="mwyA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwyQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyg">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyw">]</span></span></a></sup> interventions.</p>

<section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwzA"><h3 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Personalized_Nutrition">Personalized Nutrition</h3>
<p id="mwzQ">In 2014 Elinav discovered that people consuming identical foods and additives, such as non-nutritive sweeteners,<sup about="#mwt111" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_26-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:0-26" id="mwzg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0A">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0Q">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt114" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NNS_37-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NNS"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NNS-37"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-NNS-37" id="mw0g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw0w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1A">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1Q">]</span></span></a></sup> general foods<sup about="#mwt117" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_27-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-27"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:1-27" id="mw1g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw1w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2A">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2Q">]</span></span></a></sup> and bread,<sup about="#mwt120" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-38" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-38"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-38" id="mw2g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw2w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3A">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3Q">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt123" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:11_39-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":11"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:11-39"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:11-39" id="mw3g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw3w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4A">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4Q">]</span></span></a></sup> feature a unique and personalized glycemic response, thereby potentially explaining the lack of uniform metabolic responses to generalized dietary approaches.<sup about="#mwt126" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-40" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-40"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-40" id="mw4g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw4w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5A">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5Q">]</span></span></a></sup> Personalized dietary recommendations,<sup about="#mwt129" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-41" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-41"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-41" id="mw5g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw5w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6A">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6Q">]</span></span></a></sup> based on individualized dietary,<sup about="#mwt132" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-42" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-42"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-42" id="mw6g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7A">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7Q">]</span></span></a></sup> clinical and microbiota data, improved pre-diabetes control.<sup about="#mwt133" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_27-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:1-27" id="mw7g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw7w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8A">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8Q">]</span></span></a></sup> He similarly showed, that consumption of probiotics<sup about="#mwt136" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:12_43-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":12"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:12-43"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:12-43" id="mw8g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw8w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9A">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9Q">]</span></span></a></sup> leads to a person-specific colonization resistance and physiological patterns.<sup about="#mwt139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-44"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-44" id="mw9g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw9w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-A">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mw-g"><h3 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Nutritional_timing_and_the_Microbiota">Nutritional timing and the Microbiota</h3>
<p id="mw-w">Elinav discovered, that the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Gut_microbiota" title="Gut microbiota" id="mw_A">gut microbiota</a>  features a compositional and functional diurnal activity during a 24-hour cycle, which is dictated by host and environmental factors, mainly by the timing in food consumption.<sup about="#mwt142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-45"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-45" id="mw_Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw_g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_w">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt145" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_46-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:2-46"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:2-46" id="mwAQE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQM">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQQ">]</span></span></a></sup> These microbiota diurnal activities are tightly coordinated with the host gastrointestinal and systemic circadian activity,<sup about="#mwt148" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_47-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":4"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:4-47"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:4-47" id="mwAQU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQc">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQg">]</span></span></a></sup> while disruption of circadian activity by jet-lag<sup about="#mwt151" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-48" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-48"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-48" id="mwAQk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQs">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQw">]</span></span></a></sup> or shift work may lead to alterations in the microbiota behavior, which contribute to the development of common metabolic,<sup about="#mwt152" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_46-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:2-46" id="mwAQ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ8">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARA">]</span></span></a></sup> immune<sup about="#mwt153" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TimurT_21-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TimurT"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-TimurT-21"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-TimurT-21" id="mwARE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARM">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and liver diseases.<sup about="#mwt156" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-49" id="mwARU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARc">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_47-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":4"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-:4-47" id="mwARk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARs">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwAR0"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Awards_and_recognition">Awards and recognition</h2>
<p id="mwAR4">Elinav was awarded the Rappaport prize for biomedical research in 2015,<sup about="#mwt160" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rappaport_50-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Rappaport"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Rappaport-50"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-Rappaport-50" id="mwAR8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASE">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASI">]</span></span></a></sup> the Levinson award for basic science research in 2016,<sup about="#mwt161" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-51" id="mwASM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASU">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASY">]</span></span></a></sup> the Landau prize of Immunology in 2018<sup about="#mwt164" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-52" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-52"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-52" id="mwASc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASk">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASo">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./The_EFSD_and_the_Novo_Nordisk_Foundation_Precision_Diabetes_Medicine_Award" title="The EFSD and the Novo Nordisk Foundation Precision Diabetes Medicine Award" class="mw-redirect" id="mwASs">The EFSD and the Novo Nordisk Foundation Precision Diabetes Medicine Award</a> in 2023.<sup about="#mwt167" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-53" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-53"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-53" id="mwASw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAS0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS4">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS8">]</span></span></a></sup> Elinav was inducted into the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./European_Molecular_Biology_Organization" title="European Molecular Biology Organization" id="mwATA">European Molecular Biology Organization </a> (EMBO) in 2017,<sup about="#mwt170" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-54" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-54"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-54" id="mwATE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATM">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATQ">]</span></span></a></sup> the American Academy of Microbiology in 2021,<sup about="#mwt173" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-55" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-55"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-55" id="mwATU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATc">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATg">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./German_National_Academy_of_Sciences_Leopoldina" title="German National Academy of Sciences Leopoldina" id="mwATk">German National Academy of Sciences Leopoldina</a><sup about="#mwt176" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-56" id="mwATo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATw">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAT0">]</span></span></a></sup> and The European Academy for Cancer Sciences in 2025.<sup about="#mwt179" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-57" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-57"}}'><a href="./Eran_Elinav#cite_note-57" id="mwAT4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAT8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUA">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

